WHY GPL-3.0-OR-LATER SPECIFICALLY
---------------------------------

The version is forced by what the binary bundles, not by preference:

  * mutagen is GPL-2.0-or-later. It is copyleft, so the combined distributed
    work must be licensed under the GPL. "or-later" is what permits taking it
    under version 3.
  * requests is Apache-2.0, which is incompatible with GPLv2 but compatible
    with GPLv3.
  * PySide6 is offered as LGPL-3.0-only OR GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only. There
    is no LGPL-2.1 option, so a GPLv2 combination is not available either.

GPLv2 is therefore not a usable option for this distribution. GPL-3.0-or-later
is.

See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md for the full component list.


OBTAINING THE SOURCE CODE
-------------------------

GPLv3 section 6 requires that anyone who receives this program in binary form
can also obtain its complete corresponding source.

  Source repository:  https://github.com/VespralSquid/guitar-helper

The repository is public, which satisfies section 6(d): the corresponding source
is available from that network server, free of charge, to everyone who receives
the binary. Each release is tagged, so the source corresponding to a given build
is the tag matching its version.

No separate written offer is therefore made, or needed. If the repository ever
stops being publicly reachable, one of the other section 6 routes has to replace
it before any further binary is distributed.
